<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rāhula</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rahula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rāhula was the son of Prince Siddhārtha, later the Buddha, and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasodhara">Yaśodharā</a>. The Pāli tradition says he was born on the day of his father's renunciation, when the prince was 29, and was named for a &quot;fetter&quot; on the path; the Mūlasarvāstivāda tradition says he was conceived that day and born six years later. When the Buddha returned to his hometown, Yaśodharā had Rāhula ask for the throne of the Śākya clan, and the Buddha instead had him ordained as the first Buddhist novice monk. Early accounts state that Rāhula died before the Buddha, while later tradition holds that he outlived him. The earliest texts give little detail about him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rahula.jpg" alt="Rāhula" width="330" height="538" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rahula_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
